    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1258">

                <pb facs="0873" n="757" xml:id="pg757"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.512/412.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Brazilian Minister to
                        Mexico.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 27, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>217. Department informed that demand has been made upon American Mining and
                    Milling Company, owning Siglo XX, Dolores, Edwin E, Harriet M, mines, and Corwin
                    and Green Consolidated Mining and Milling Company, owning Esperanza, Meliza and
                    Ana Maria, mines; all located in La Luz Mineral District, Guanajuato, for
                    repayment of taxes already paid by them to agents of Huerta administration.</p>
                <p>Please bring to attention of General Carranza and request the issuance of orders
                    against the exaction from these American corporations of taxes which they have
                    already paid to persons exercising de facto authority. Since time limit for
                    payment demanded expires August 31, orders in question should be issued
                    immediately.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
